  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Counter-Trafficking Response in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea can significantly benefit from support to align the national legal and regulatory framework with international human rights protection standards for victims and potential victims of trafficking and other vulnerable groups. The project aims to support the Government&apos;s efforts in better preparing for accession to the UN Convention on Transnational Organized Crime (UNTOC) and the Protocol to Prevent, Suppress and Punish Trafficking in Persons, Especially Women and Children (TIP Protocol).</narrative>
  </description>
